n\nHmm, `_search_regex` might call `self._downloader.report_warning` on failure. With default provided, it returns default without warning. With fatal, raises ExtractorError. Since we provide matching webpages, fine.\n\nNow, `unified_timestamp` \u2014 real; needs a parseable date string. E.g., '2020-01-01T00:00:00Z' or 'Jan 1, 2020'. Let me use ISO format.\n\n`parse_duration` \u2014 real; '5:00' \u2192 300.\n\n`clean_html` \u2014 real.\n\n`urljoin` \u2014 real.\n\nNow let me design the webpages.\n\n### Test 1: Single video with lesson JSON\n\nURL: needs to match `_VALID_URL` with chapter_id and lesson_id groups but not course_id. Based on my memory of the valid URL, a URL like `https://linuxacademy.com/cp/modules/view/id/1234` would match chapter_id group with id '1234'. But I need to verify the actual regex. Let me use get_info.\n\nActually, let me look at the real youtube-dl source for linuxacademy.py. I recall it fairly well now:\n\n```python\nclass LinuxAcademyIE(InfoExtractor):\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                    https?://\n                        (?:\n                            (?:www\\.)?linuxacademy\\.com/|\n                            cdn\\.linuxacademy\\.com/\n                        )\n                        (?:\n                            (?P<course_id>cp/courses/view/course/)|\n                            (?P<chapter_id>cp/modules/view/id/)|\n                            (?P<lesson_id>education/courses/course/)\n                        )\n                        (?P<id>[^/?#&]+)\n                    '''\n```\n\nHmm wait, but then for a single video, item_id = '%s-%s' % (chapter_id, lecture_id) = e.g. 'cp/modules/view/id-1234'? That seems odd. Let me think again...\n\nActually I found it. The real source from youtube-dl:\n\n```python\nclass LinuxAcademyIE(InfoExtractor):\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                    https?://\n                        (?:\n                            (?:www\\.)?linuxacademy\\.com/|\n                       